== a file on your opponent
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: council candidate | parliamentary candidate
per_year: 0 0 .12 .12 .12 .12
drivers: unrest+.2 stress+.1
times: per candidate: about 1 campaign in 10 is offered damaging material on a rival, more in close races (estimate)
likelier: a close race, a bitter local feud, a rival with a business or a long public past, a hostile press
rarer: a safe seat, a small village contest, a rival with a short, quiet life
gap: 1-3
domain: career.3 community.3
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: week
roles: rival, friend, colleague, boss
earth: an envelope of documents about the other candidate
tribal: a woman tells you the rival's speaker once broke a hunting oath
magic: a sealed packet of letters that would ruin your rival, if they are real
scene: A brown envelope arrives at the campaign office with no name on it. Inside are copies of letters about {rival}'s business: a debt, a court date, a name {N} does not recognise.
scene W: There are proper ways to raise a concern about a candidate, and an anonymous envelope is not one of them. {N} holds it at arm's length.
scene U: {N} reads every page twice. Some of it might be true; some of it looks too neat. Who gains from {N} having this?
scene B: {N} weighs the envelope in one hand. Used well, it could end {rival}'s campaign in a week.
scene R: {N} feels sick, then angry. This is not the fight {N} signed up for.
scene G: {N} has known {rival}'s family for years, on the same streets and at the same school gates. Whatever is in here, they still live here.
scene tribal: A woman comes to {Ns} hearth after dark and says that {rival} once broke a hunting oath, and she can name who saw it.
scene magic: A sealed packet of letters is left at {Ns} door. If they are real they would ruin {rival}; if they are forged they would ruin whoever uses them.
- W | hand the envelope unopened to the officer who runs the election | v: conformity | tribal: take the woman to the elders, and let them hear it | magic: hand the packet unopened to the Order's warden of the lots | chance: 88
- U | check every document before deciding anything, and take nothing at face value | v: achievement, security | tribal: ask quietly who else saw the oath broken, before deciding anything | magic: have the seals and the hands checked before deciding anything | chance: 90
- B | keep the file in the safe, in case it is ever needed | v: power | tribal: remember the tale, and keep it for a day it might be needed | magic: lock the packet away, in case it is ever needed | chance: 86
- R | throw the envelope in the bin, and win clean or not at all | self_control: + | v: stimulation, universalism | tribal: send the woman away, and win clean or not at all | magic: throw the packet in the fire, and win clean or not at all | chance: 93
- G | leave it in the drawer, since the town knows the rival's family well enough | v: tradition | tribal: leave it be, since the band knows the rival's family well enough | magic: leave it in the drawer, since the ward knows the rival's house well enough | chance: 80
- BG | leak it through an old friend on the local paper, with nothing to link it back | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: an anonymous smear; backfire: the leak is traced back, and the story becomes one about the leaker | self_control: - | v: power, tradition | tribal: let the tale slip to an old friend among the singers, with nothing to link it back | magic: pass the letters to an old friend at a broadsheet, with nothing to link them back | chance: 76
- UG | find out who sent it, and why, before doing anything else | v: security, self-direction | tribal: find out who sent the woman, and why, before doing anything else | chance: 66
- UR | raise it in the next debate, on the record and to the rival's face | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: using unchecked papers against a rival; backfire: the rival sues for defamation | v: stimulation, power | tribal: say it at the next fire, in front of the rival and the whole band | magic: raise it at the next dispute on the steps, to the rival's face | chance: 60
- WB | pass it to the party's lawyers, and let them decide whether it can be used | v: conformity, security | tribal: pass it to the faction's elders, and let them decide what to do with it | magic: pass it to the faction's advocates, and let them decide whether it can be used | chance: 72
- WR | warn the rival that someone is passing a file around | mark: made a friend | v: universalism, benevolence | tribal: warn the rival that a tale is going round the hearths | magic: warn the rival that someone is hawking letters about them | chance: 62
