scene: The division bell rings at seven. The bill in front of the chamber is one {N} thinks is wrong, and {boss} has been clear: the party votes for it, and the party remembers who does not.
scene W: {N} stood on the party's platform and owes it loyalty. {N} also owes the people who voted, and tonight the two pull apart.
scene U: {N} has read every clause. Two of them will not do what the minister says they will, and {N} can show why.
scene B: A vote is worth something to the whips tonight, and {N} knows it. The only question is what to ask for.
scene R: {N} feels it in the stomach: this is wrong. Voting for it would mean looking away from something {N} believes.
scene G: {N} thinks of the town back home, the people the bill will touch, the faces at the Friday surgery.
scene tribal: The faction will stand behind a raid on the hill people at the gathering. {N} thinks it will start a blood feud that lasts for generations.
scene magic: The faction will vote to hand the old forest to the Order, and {N} knows what lives there, and what the forest keeps out.
