age: 25-95
holds: party leader
per_year: 0 0 0 .15 .15 .15
drivers: unrest+.3 trouble+.2 prosper-.2
times: per party leader a year: about 15 in 100; most leaders leave after a defeat or a revolt (estimate)
likelier: bad polls, a lost election, a scandal, rivals with a following of their own, years in the job
rarer: a leader newly chosen, a leader who has just won, a united party
gap: 1-3
domain: career.5
tone: trouble
