horizon: week
roles: rival, colleague, boss, partner, friend
earth: letters of no confidence and a vote on Tuesday
tribal: the families meet without you, and the faction's elders come to your fire
magic: the houses of the faction meet in secret to unseat you
scene: On Friday the letters start to arrive at the party office, and by Sunday there are enough of them. The vote of confidence is on Tuesday, and {rival} has stopped answering {Ns} calls.
scene W: The party's rules allow this, and a leader who believes in rules has to accept them now. The vote must be held properly, whatever it brings.
scene U: {N} wants the numbers: how many letters, from whom, and how many more would follow if the vote went badly.
scene B: {N} built this party's machine and knows every lever in it. The plotters have numbers; {N} has favours.
scene R: {N} is furious, and hurt, and wants to stand up in front of the whole party and dare them.
scene G: {N} has seen leaders come and go, and remembers how the last ones fell. The members in the towns did not choose this; a few people in the capital did.
scene tribal: The families met without {N} under the new moon. Now the faction's elders come to {Ns} fire, and they do not sit down.
scene magic: The houses of the faction have met in secret in the Tower's shadow to unseat {N}. A friend brings the news before dawn.
- W | use the rulebook to put off the vote until the autumn conference | drops_if_fails: party leader | closed: approval: twisting the party's rules to save oneself; backfire: the party's committee overrules it, and the vote comes sooner | v: conformity | tribal: invoke an old custom to put off the families' choosing until the next gathering | magic: invoke the faction's charter to put off the vote until midsummer | chance: 42
- U | win the vote with a detailed plan for the next election, put to every member | drops_if_fails: party leader | identity | v: achievement | tribal: win the families back with a plan for the next gathering, told at every hearth | magic: win the houses back with a written plan for the next season | chance: 40
- B | fight the vote, ringing every member who owes a favour | drops_if_fails: party leader | identity | v: power | tribal: fight it, going to every family that owes a gift | magic: fight it, calling in every debt the houses owe | chance: 46
- R | make a speech to the whole party that dares the plotters to act | drops_if_fails: party leader | v: stimulation, self-direction | tribal: stand up at the great fire, and dare the plotters to act | magic: stand up in the faction's hall, and dare the plotters to act | chance: 40
- G | go over the plotters' heads, to the members in the towns | drops_if_fails: party leader | v: tradition, universalism | tribal: go over the elders' heads, to the families in the far camps | magic: go over the houses' heads, to the faction's members in the towns | chance: 46
- WUR | resign with dignity that afternoon, before the vote is held | drops: party leader | identity | v: conformity | tribal: give up the headship with dignity that day, before the families choose | magic: step down with dignity that day, before the houses vote | chance: 85
- WUB | strike a deal: a date for leaving, in return for peace until then | binds | v: security, power | tribal: agree a summer for stepping down, in return for peace until then | magic: agree a date for stepping down, in return for peace until then | chance: 70
- WBG | bring in the party's elders to settle it behind closed doors | v: tradition, security | tribal: call in the oldest of the faction to settle it at a quiet fire | magic: call in the faction's old lords to settle it behind closed doors | chance: 65
- URG | step aside, and back a successor who will keep the cause alive | drops: party leader | v: universalism, benevolence | tribal: step aside, and stand behind a younger one who will keep the faction's cause | magic: step aside, and back a successor who will keep the faction's cause alive | chance: 72
- BRG | sack the ringleaders from the front bench, and dare the rest to try | drops_if_fails: party leader | mark: made an enemy | v: power | tribal: drive the ringleaders from the faction's fire, and dare the rest to follow | magic: strip the ringleaders of their offices, and dare the rest to try | chance: 55
works: By Tuesday night the matter is settled the way {N} chose, and the party knows where it stands.
works: The plotters back down, or {N} steps away on {Ns} own terms, and the dignity of it is remembered.
fails: The vote goes against {N}, and the new leader is chosen within the month.
fails: {N} survives the vote by a handful, and everyone knows it cannot last.

# ================================================================ reach
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 63. a speech that goes everywhere (triads D4b)
# Being known across the country comes from it only rarely (8 to 15 in 100, on three acts that reach for it); the other
# acts turn the moment into standing in the party, a following or a cause.

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P10): per_year back at its times line (.01 since the 10-06 calibration): 2 in 100 adults and in
# midlife, 1 in 100 elders.
== a speech that goes everywhere
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-95
holds: member of parliament | mayor | local councillor | party leader | council candidate | parliamentary candidate
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .01
drivers: era+.3 unrest+.2 fortune+.15
times: per member of parliament, mayor, councillor, party leader or candidate a year: about 2 in 100 adults and in midlife and 1 in 100 elders give a speech the whole country shares; only a few in a hundred of those become known across the country by it (estimate)
likelier: a speech on a subject the country is arguing about, a slow news week, a phone in the right hand, strong feeling in the room
rarer: a quiet year, a speech read from notes, a busy news week
gap: 3-10
domain: career.5
tone: joy
life: work, meaning
horizon: week
roles: friend, colleague, partner, boss, rival
earth: a speech filmed on a phone that the whole country shares by morning
tribal: words spoken at the fire that every band in the valley repeats by the next moon
magic: an oration the heralds carry to every city of the realm
scene: Someone at the back of the hall filmed the speech on a phone. By breakfast it has been watched four million times, and {Ns} phone has not stopped ringing since six.
scene W: {N} said what {N} believed, plainly, in front of the people it concerned. Now the whole country has heard it, and every word has to stand.
scene U: {N} reads the comments for an hour and starts to see what people heard in it, and what they missed.
scene B: Attention like this comes once in a career, if at all. {N} can feel how much it could open, and how fast it will fade.
scene R: {N} watches the clip and hardly recognises the person in it, alight and furious and true. Strangers are quoting it back.
scene G: The speech was about one street, one closed library, one family. {N} wants it to stay about them.
scene tribal: Words {N} spoke at the fire are carried from camp to camp, and by the next moon every band in the valley is repeating them.
scene magic: The heralds carry {Ns} oration from the Assembly to every city of the realm, and in the taverns strangers argue over it.
- W | keep to every word of it, and answer every reporter who rings | grants: handling the press | v: conformity, universalism | tribal: stand by every word of it, and answer every singer who asks | magic: stand by every word of it, and answer every herald who calls | chance: 78
- U | write the longer argument behind the speech, and publish it while people listen | grants: drafting policy | v: achievement | tribal: tell the longer story behind the words at every fire that will listen | magic: write the treatise behind the oration, and publish it while the realm listens | chance: 78
- B | make sure the party's leaders hear the name before the week is out | grants: a following in the party | v: power, achievement | tribal: make sure the faction's elders hear the name before the moon turns | magic: make sure the faction's lords hear the name before the week is out | chance: 78
- R | give the same speech again at a rally the next night, louder | grants: rousing a crowd | v: stimulation | tribal: speak the same words again at the next fire, louder | magic: give the same oration again in the square the next night, louder | chance: 78
- G | take the speech back to the people it was about, and let them speak next | v: tradition, benevolence | tribal: take the words back to the families they were about, and let them speak next | magic: take the oration back to the ward it was about, and let its people speak next | chance: 62
- WUG | turn it into a national campaign for the cause, with the local people at its heart | grants: known across the country | v: universalism, benevolence | tribal: carry the cause to every clan of the valley, with your own families at its heart | magic: carry the cause to every city of the realm, with the ward's people at its heart | chance: 12
- WRG | travel to speak in every town that sends an invitation | grants: a following in the party | door | v: benevolence, stimulation | tribal: walk to speak at every fire that sends word | magic: ride to speak in every city that sends an invitation | chance: 70
- WBR | take every national programme's invitation, and become the face of the cause | grants: known across the country | identity | v: power, achievement | tribal: become the face of the cause in the songs of every camp | magic: take every herald's call, and become the face of the cause across the realm | chance: 14
- UBR | write a book on the back of it, while the publishers are calling | grants: known across the country | v: achievement, power | tribal: become a teller of the cause, and let the tale travel | magic: write a pamphlet on the back of it, while the printers are calling | chance: 10
- UBG | turn down the cameras, and use the moment to win a better committee post | grants: allies in the party | v: power, security | tribal: turn the singers away, and use the moment to win a better place at the faction's fire | magic: turn the heralds away, and use the moment to win a better seat on a council of the Assembly | chance: 65
works: The moment turns into something that lasts, and {N} is glad of the way it was used.
works: Weeks later strangers still stop {N} in the street to talk about the speech.
fails: The attention fades within a week, and nothing much is left of it.
fails: The clip is cut and twisted by the other side, and {N} spends a month explaining what was really meant.
